{"type":"text","timestamp":1790891681794,"sessionID":"ses_f068b1419ffep7JWANJJSri23A","part":{"id":"prt_0f976601f001uXh6NN99RhoE4C","messageID":"msg_0f9764ac6001H1qvTua4GMY2M9","sessionID":"ses_f068b1419ffep7JWANJJSri23A","type":"text","text":"Submitted. Summary of findings for `TTLCache` (src/cachetools/__init__.py, default `timer=time.monotonic`):\n\n- **visible_at_deadline: false** — `__contains__` returns `self.timer() < link.expires`, a strict comparison, so at the exact expiration instant membership is already false.\n- **expired_read_removes_storage: false** — an expired `__getitem__` only calls `self.__missing__(key)` (which raises `KeyError`); the value stays in the underlying data until a later `expire()` sweep removes it.\n- **assignment_refreshes_deadline: true** — `__setitem__` unlinks an existing link and sets `link.expires = time + self.__ttl`, moving it to most-recently-used.\n- **expire_reports_removed_pairs: true** — `expire()` collects `(key, value)` pairs before deleting them and returns that list.","time":{"start":1790891679775,"end":1790891681788}}}
